18:22:49.049  === WHERE DOES THE LINE CHANGE BELONG? ===
18:22:49.052  The delay does not matter - 0 to 150 ms all gave the same thing. So the question
18:22:49.052  is not when we switch but whether the cable's reply to 0x83F0 comes before or
18:22:49.052  after its own switch. Three arrangements, same bytes in all of them.

18:22:49.071    --- variant 1: switch, then read the 0x83F0 reply at 9600 (what we do now)
18:22:50.380        0xA77A  -> 77 07 77 07 77 07 70
18:22:50.986        0xB318  -> 77 07 77 07 77 07 70
18:22:51.718        0x83F0  -> 25 09 02
18:22:52.625        0x46F1  -> C4 F0 C4 B8 FF

18:22:52.627    --- variant 2: read the 0x83F0 reply at 19200, then switch, then query at 9600
18:22:53.934        0xA77A  -> 77 07 77 07 77 07 70
18:22:54.539        0xB318  -> 77 07 77 07 77 07 70
18:22:55.244        0x83F0  -> 77 07 77 07 77 07 70
18:22:56.156        0x46F1  -> C4 F0 C4 B8 FF

18:22:56.157    --- variant 3: never switch; everything at 19200
